a las vegas doctor readjusting to life  in the states again after spending  months volunteering in ukraine tonight  he spoke with victoria saha on why he  wanted to be there despite the ongoing  war with russia  the images of the destruction ukraine is  facing did not scare dr wilson bernalis  instead it pushed him to volunteer his  medical skills it was a harrowing dr  bernalis a family practitioner in the  las vegas area describes what he saw  firsthand when he was in ukraine the  devastation we were seeing on tv was  just a sliver of what he was facing this  old lady  with 21 bullet fragments  and we have to take them out  one by one in the in the office  you know and then we we asked her if she  wants to go to the hospital she said no  you know she was so frantic to get out  of ukraine  he said no no no i'm going to poland in  an undisclosed secret shelter dr  bernalis was stationed near the border  of poland where refugees would stop  before continuing their journey this  defenseless citizen especially women and  children  and i don't know how blood president  vladimir putin's sleep at night but the  crying screaming and panic dr bernalis  faced from the refugees trying to escape  ukraine was starting to affect him  earlier this month he decided to come  back home i felt a lot of guilt coming  home  you know but  i said  you know i did my part i was there for  three and a half months victoria saha  live local now  the doctor says he would like to return  to ukraine eventually and he encourages  other american doctors to help out as  well
 

